framework ArchitectureDecisionRecord:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain ADR0023:
  description |
    pair.sight and pair.sound are not unique two-person cognition.
    Physical LOS and observer projection read organ, exposure, and
    placement facts. Stored sight/sound keys remain a derived fill.

problem P1:
  |
    ADR-0022 stopped engine revalidation from reading observer
    frames, but unique world still hosts a mutual sight/sound
    channel that engine LOS, visual projection, and utterance
    hearing treat as authority.

premise DRIVER_UNIQUE:
  |
    Unique world may hold placements, topology geometry, body
    facing, organ vision and hearing, exposure, illumination,
    area noise, object sensory effects, and a mechanical distance
    band.

premise DRIVER_TWO_FRAMES:
  |
    Two-person perceptual relations live only in the two observer
    frames. A single pair.sight or pair.sound is not those frames
    and is not unique world cognition.

premise DRIVER_SCOPE:
  |
    Do not delete pairRelations, distance, or orientations. Do not
    drop sight/sound keys from stored JSON in this slice. Do not
    fast-forward hops. Mental-effect routing stays open.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Considered options are: leave pair.sight/sound as authority;
    stop reading them now and keep a derived fill on write; or
    delete the keys in the same slice. Leaving them as authority
    keeps the mix-in. Deleting keys rewrites parse of in-flight
    battles. Stop-reading plus derived fill is the producing
    repair.

evidence E_OWNER:
  |
    On 2026-09-06 the product owner, after ADR-0022, instructed to
    tidy the remaining mix-in. Analysis:
    docs/remaining-pair-channel-mix-in.llmthink.dsl.

evidence E_READS:
  |
    packages/shared/src/action-feasibility.ts uses pair.sight for
    line_of_sight_blocked. perception-projection.ts uses pair.sight
    blocked and partial. utterance-perception.ts uses pair.sound
    blocked and partial.

evidence E_UNIQUE:
  |
    deriveBattleActorCausality already folds object visionEffect and
    hearingEffect into effectiveActorState. Exposure, organ
    vision/hearing, illumination, and area noise already exist.

decision D1 based_on P1, DRIVER_UNIQUE, DRIVER_TWO_FRAMES, E_READS:
  |
    Engine LOS, visual counterpart projection, and utterance
    hearing must not read pair.sight or pair.sound. Physical LOS
    uses organ vision including causality-derived vision, and
    exposure. Observer visual none uses absence, separate_area,
    out_of_scene, hidden or invisible, or blocked/absent vision.
    Hearing uses organ hearing, distance, area noise, and
    utterance properties.

decision D2 based_on DRIVER_SCOPE, OPTIONS, E_UNIQUE:
  |
    Keep pair.distance and orientations. Keep sight/sound keys on
    the schema as a derived compatibility fill from presence and
    same-area. They are not authority. Deleting the keys is a
    later parse migration.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-06 the product owner instructed to tidy the
    remaining mix-in after ADR-0022.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on D1, D2, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE, E_OWNER:
  |
    ADR-0023 is Accepted at this owner-approved revision.
    Implementation of D1 and D2 is authorized. ADR-0020, ADR-0021,
    and ADR-0022 remain Accepted.
